`; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/claimability.py:160 `getattr(cfg, 'runner', None)`","Plan: 'Fires ONLY on zero references (the bug condition), so refactors that move reads cannot FP'","Field-name collisions across sections (threshold in ticket_clarity+compact; enforce_since in identity) make section binding load-bearing"],"finding":"The `cfg.<section>.<field>` two-segment attribute-chain match will false-flag live, genuinely-read fields whose reads go through a bound section object or getattr, contradicting the plan's 'zero-reference-only / refactors cannot FP' guarantee.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff85c32b8747b69e0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('require >=1 attribute-read site (cfg.<section>.<field>)'); Acceptance Criteria line 3 ('Zero-reference-only firing')","norm_id":"n3f5aa978ce59e16e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A field read only via `sect = cfg.<section>` then `sect.<field>` is reported inert though it is honored at runtime","compact.threshold and compact.COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS both flagged despite compact.py reading them"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have the walk track local names bound to a `.<section>` attribute (and section-typed parameters) and count `<local>.<field>` reads against that section; treat `getattr(<section-obj>, '<field>')` string literals as reads too.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the AST check recognizes a config read regardless of receiver variable name (e.g. match on any `.<section>.<field>` attribute chain, or resolve the config object's binding), so aliased/parameter-bound reads are not misclassified as zero-read.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'require >=1 attribute-read site (cfg.<section>.<field>) outside the schema/config plumbing modules'","AST match must know which receiver expressions count as the config object; unstated in plan"],"finding":"The read-site detection pattern 'cfg.<section>.<field>' assumes a fixed receiver identifier ('cfg'), but the plan does not state how the AST walk identifies a read when the config object is bound to a different name (self.config, settings, an aliased import, or passed as a parameter). An AST attribute-read match keyed only on the literal 'cfg' prefix would miss legitimate reads under other receiver names and FP-fire on genuinely-read fields.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda91ae881db7fa4d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'require >=1 attribute-read site (cfg.<section>.<field>)'","norm_id":"n5710b1a457011f15","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A field read via `self._config.section.field` or a locally-aliased config object is reported as zero-read and fails CI despite being used"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State the match rule: detect any attribute-access chain ending in `.<section>.<field>` for known section/field pairs, independent of the base identifier, OR enumerate the accepted config receiver names.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate (or give a concrete path/glob rule for) the schema/config plumbing modules excluded from read-site counting.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'outside the schema/config plumbing modules' — set left undefined","Only '_config_schema.py' is named explicitly"],"finding":"The plan does not name the set of modules that constitute 'schema/config plumbing' (the excluded read sites). Without an enumerated exclusion list, an executor cannot deterministically decide which files are ignored when counting read sites.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff678c32815d58d4b","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'outside the schema/config plumbing modules'","norm_id":"n29acf65e584d3cad","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A config-loader or validation module that legitimat